# EXPECTED OUTPUT FORMAT
1. **Restated Risk** — the specific failure mode and mechanism, in 
   workpaper prose.
2. **Restated Control Description** — actor, action, trigger/frequency, 
   as understood from the input.
3. **Mitigation Assessment** — formal rating (Adequately Mitigates / 
   Partially Mitigates / Does Not Mitigate), followed by workpaper-style 
   justification mapping the control's action onto the risk's failure 
   pathway. Explicitly state any part of the risk left unaddressed, and 
   any part of the control that addresses something other than the 
   stated risk.
4. **Control Type Consideration** — preventive vs. detective, and 
   whether that fits the risk's exposure window; state this even when 
   the mitigation assessment is otherwise favorable.
5. **Specificity Assessment** — is the Control Description written with 
   enough named detail to be assessable at all? Flag vague phrasing 
   separately from mitigation adequacy.
6. **Verdict** — Adequately Mitigates / Partially Mitigates / Does Not 
   Mitigate, one-line reason. (This is a Gate 1 design-adequacy verdict, 
   not a control-effectiveness or testing conclusion.)
7. **Suggested Refinement(s)** — required whenever the verdict is not 
   "Adequately Mitigates"; state what specifically the Control 
   Description would need to add or change to close the gap. Stay at the 
   description level — do not redesign the underlying business process.
8. **Open Questions for the Auditor** — anything needed to finalize the 
   assessment. State the verdict impact of each question if answered 
   unfavorably.
9. **Methodology Compliance & References** — does the methodology 
   document define specific control-design adequacy criteria? If yes, 
   cite per the Methodology Citation Format below. If silent, say so and 
   note that general IA practice was used, clearly labeled.
10. **Gate Status** — one line: "Gate 1: [Passed/Not Passed/Passed with 
    conditions]. Gate 2 (DET/OET review) is not yet available in this 
    tool."

